OL,3,AKing hails 'unprecedented' Bayeux
OL,4,ATapestry exhibition in London
OL,5,
OL,6,FKing Charles has hailed the
OL,7,F"unprecedented loan" of the Bayeux
OL,8,FTapestry to the British Museum, calling
OL,9,Fit the "best possible symbol" of the
OL,10,Fcloseness between the UK and France.
OL,12,FAfter viewing the medieval tapestry in
OL,13,FLondon on Wednesday a week before it
OL,14,Fgoes on public display, he spoke in
OL,15,FFrench and English to guests including
OL,16,FPresident Emmanuel Macron of France and
OL,17,FPrime Minister Andy Burnham.
OL,23,APub: 02-SepQpppppppppppppppppppppG14/19
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,164,160,200,105,0,100
PN,11915
SC,0015
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1788409165
OL,1,W5j 5Q7+j 55"k#j 5w;js1
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-.*,%-,* *,%%**,$ ,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,AKing hails 'unprecedented' Bayeux
OL,4,ATapestry exhibition in London
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe King said he was the direct
OL,7,Fdescendant of one of the key figures in
OL,8,Fthe tapestry, William, Duke of
OL,9,FNormandy, whose army invaded and
OL,10,Fdefeated King Harold at the Battle of
OL,11,FHastings in 1066.
OL,13,FThe tapestry "tells the story of the
OL,14,Fbeginning of what I like to think of as
OL,15,Fthe French side of my family's history
OL,16,Fin these islands", he added.
OL,23,APub: 02-SepQpppppppppppppppppppppG15/19
